    "limitations": [
      "This is an observed geometric envelope for the 150 vertices in one accepted captured state, not a formal upper bound over all shader inputs or arithmetic paths.",
      "It does not bound times between captures or prove continuous-time separation.",
      "Exact native intersections remain recorded; no gate, tolerance, or source geometry is changed.",
      "Tangential intersection span is reported separately from signed normal-side intrusion; a long span is not a penetration depth."
    ],
    "pair_bound": "The distance between two triangle sets can change by at most the sum of their Hausdorff bounds. Thus an observed captured intersection implies the ideal triangle pair had separation no larger than epsilon_A+epsilon_B. Exact point intersections in the ideal map have zero separation by definition.",
    "per_triangle_bound": "For corresponding vertex errors e_i, any equal-barycentric point has error norm <= sum(lambda_i*e_i) <= max_i(e_i); therefore the actual-vs-ideal triangle Hausdorff distance is bounded by the largest vertex error."
